    <!-- Issue #332: org.jetbrains.kotlin:kotlin-stdlib (CVE-2026-53914, NVD-rated 9.8 CRITICAL)
         — CONFIRMED FALSE POSITIVE, verified directly against the NVD detail page
         (nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-53914) on 2026-07-09. The vulnerability is "unsafe
         deserialization in the build cache metadata" (CWE-502) — a Kotlin BUILD SYSTEM/compiler
         tooling flaw (Gradle build cache), fixed in Kotlin 2.4.20. This project does not run the
         Kotlin compiler or Gradle build cache at all — kotlin-stdlib is consumed purely as a
         runtime dependency (transitively via okhttp, used by razorpay-java). The vulnerable code
         path (build cache metadata deserialization) is not present in kotlin-stdlib.jar and is
         never invoked by this project's usage. dependency-check's CPE match
         (cpe:2.3:a:jetbrains:kotlin:*, no version bound) covers the whole JetBrains Kotlin
         product family (compiler + build tooling + stdlib) as one CPE, which is the documented
         false-positive class for coarse-grained project-level CPEs
         (dependency-check.github.io docs; also see arxiv.org/pdf/1808.09753). Already on latest
         stable kotlin-stdlib (2.4.0) independent of this suppression. -->
    <suppress>
        <notes>Confirmed false positive, verified against NVD directly — CVE-2026-53914 is a
        Kotlin build-cache-metadata deserialization flaw (compiler/Gradle tooling), not a
        kotlin-stdlib runtime issue; this project never runs Kotlin build tooling, only consumes
        the compiled stdlib jar at runtime. See issue #332.</notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.jetbrains\.kotlin/kotlin-stdlib.*@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-53914</cve>
    </suppress>

    <!-- Issue #332: io.micrometer:micrometer-registry-prometheus (CVE-2026-42154, 7.5 HIGH) —
         CONFIRMED FALSE POSITIVE, verified directly against the NVD detail page on 2026-07-09.
         The vulnerability is in the Prometheus SERVER's own /api/v1/read remote-read endpoint
         (unvalidated snappy-decompressed length -> unbounded memory allocation, CWE-400/770/789),
         fixed in Prometheus 3.5.3/3.11.3. This project does not run a Prometheus server —
         micrometer-registry-prometheus is a client-side metrics-exposition library that formats
         metrics for an external Prometheus server to scrape; it does not implement or expose the
         remote-read API at all. dependency-check's CPE match
         (cpe:2.3:a:prometheus:prometheus:*, no version bound) is a vendor/product name collision
         with the actual Prometheus server product, triggered by "prometheus" appearing in the
         artifact name. Already on latest stable version (1.17.0) independent of this
         suppression. -->
    <suppress>
        <notes>Confirmed false positive, verified against NVD directly — CVE-2026-42154 is in the
        Prometheus server's /api/v1/read endpoint; micrometer-registry-prometheus is a
        client-side exposition library with no such endpoint. Vendor/product name collision
        ("prometheus" in artifact name). See issue #332.</notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/io\.micrometer/micrometer-registry-prometheus@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-42154</cve>
    </suppress>

    <!-- Issue #332: io.netty:* 4.1.136.Final family (CVE-2026-42582, 7.5 HIGH) — CONFIRMED
         FALSE POSITIVE, verified directly against the NVD detail page on 2026-07-09. The
         vulnerability is in the QPACK header decoder (io.netty.handler.codec.http3.QpackDecoder),
         part of netty-codec-http3, affecting versions 4.2.0.Alpha1 through 4.2.12.Final (fixed in
         4.2.13.Final). This project is on netty 4.1.136.Final — an entirely different major.minor
         line, outside the affected 4.2.x range — and does not depend on netty-codec-http3 at all
         (no HTTP/3 usage anywhere). dependency-check's CPE match (cpe:2.3:a:netty:netty:*, no
         version bound) covers the whole Netty product as one CPE regardless of module — a real CI
         run first surfaced this on netty-codec-4.1.136.Final.jar, a sibling module to
         netty-transport/netty-transport-native-unix-common (originally suppressed) that a local
         run's NVD snapshot hadn't flagged; broadened from an artifactId-prefix match to cover the
         whole io.netty groupId at this CVE, since the false-positive reasoning (4.1.x has no
         HTTP/3 support anywhere in the release) applies uniformly across every netty-* module
         shipped from the same 4.1.136.Final release, not just the specific ones observed so far. -->
    <suppress>
        <notes>Confirmed false positive, verified against NVD directly — CVE-2026-42582 only
        affects Netty 4.2.0.Alpha1-4.2.12.Final's HTTP/3 QPACK decoder (netty-codec-http3); this
        project is on netty 4.1.136.Final (different major line, outside the affected range, no
        HTTP/3 support at all). Covers the whole io.netty groupId at this CVE — applies uniformly
        across every module shipped from the same 4.1.136.Final release. See issue #332.</notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/io\.netty/.*@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-42582</cve>
    </suppress>

