    <!-- PR #686 (extended #133 re-run, 2026-08-07): org.apache.tomcat.embed:* 10.1.57
         (CVE-2026-66299, 7.5 HIGH) — CONFIRMED FALSE POSITIVE, verified directly against
         Apache's own advisory (tomcat.apache.org/security-10.html) and NVD on 2026-08-06. The
         vulnerability is an unbounded-buffer DoS in the bundled WebSocket **chat example**
         application shipped with the full Tomcat binary distribution's webapps/examples
         directory — Apache's own advisory states installs that removed the examples web
         application (standard hardening guidance) are not affected. Spring Boot's embedded
         Tomcat (spring-boot-starter-tomcat, which is what this project uses via
         spring-boot-starter-web) never packages or deploys the examples web application at all —
         it is not a Maven artifact and is not present anywhere in this project's resolved
         dependency tree or runtime classpath. This applies equally to every org.apache.tomcat.embed
         artifact this project resolves (tomcat-embed-core, tomcat-embed-websocket, etc.) — the
         false-positive reasoning is about the absent examples webapp, not about which specific
         embedded-Tomcat jar is on the classpath, so the rule below is scoped to the whole group
         rather than one artifact at a time. Widened from tomcat-embed-core-only after a #133
         CI re-run surfaced the identical CVE flagged against tomcat-embed-websocket, which the
         original narrower regex didn't cover. No patched version is needed or exists as a fix
         for this specific finding: 10.1.57 remains the latest release published to Maven Central
         as of this writing (confirmed against Maven Central's maven-metadata.xml — no 10.1.58
         artifact exists there yet despite third-party vulnerability-database pages citing one as
         "the fix"). -->
    <suppress>
        <notes>Confirmed false positive, verified against Apache's own tomcat.apache.org
        security-10.html advisory and NVD directly — CVE-2026-66299 is a DoS in the bundled
        WebSocket chat example web application (webapps/examples in the full Tomcat
        distribution), which Spring Boot's embedded Tomcat never packages or deploys. Not present
        anywhere in this project's dependency tree or runtime classpath. Scoped to the whole
        org.apache.tomcat.embed group (not just tomcat-embed-core) since the false-positive
        reasoning applies to every artifact in it equally. See PR #686.</notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.apache\.tomcat\.embed/.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-66299</cve>
    </suppress>

